      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1.17‑kilometre stretch hosts 37 officially protected historic buildings, a testament to its French Concession heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wukang_Road",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "At the southern end, the Wukang Mansion—designed by Hungarian architect László Hudec in 1924—stands as Shanghai’s ship‑shaped landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://urbanchinatravelogue.com/wukang-road-and-anfu-road-shanghai/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tree‑lined streets here blend old‑world villas with trendy cafés and independent boutiques, creating a lively modern vibe.",
